// How items sit in a survivor's hand (read by the client: crates/client/src/held.rs).
//
// Anything held is drawn in the hand's grip frame: the grip at the origin, on the palm (4 cm out
// of the hand's middle, so a handle lies on the palm's skin, not through the hand); the item
// pointing along +Z, out past the thumb; its top +Y, toward the wrist; so +X is out of the right
// palm, and for the left hand out of its back. A gun is the same turned a quarter: its barrel on
// the way the fingers point, its top to the thumb. The hand is turned to hold it that way
// (`survivor_model::Hand`). A held model is made that way; an item with only a ground model, or
// none, is laid along +Z and centred on the grip. A grip here then moves the item
// in that frame (`offset`, metres), turns it (`turn`, degrees about X, then Y, then Z) and scales
// it (`scale`), so an item that sits wrong is put right without code. Every field is optional.
//
// A release build's models have grips of their own (release-models/held/grips.ron), read over
// these, since a grip belongs to the model it fits.
//
//   "kitchen_knife": (offset: (0.0, 0.0, -0.02), turn: (0.0, 0.0, 90.0), scale: 1.0),
//
// Food being eaten with no entry here is moved out of the face by `held::EATING`; an entry
// replaces that (these two were tuned against the eating clip, which lays the left palm on the
// mouth: on the palm the food is inside the head, so it is drawn on the back of the hand, +X).
{
    "tinned_beans": (offset: (0.12, 0.0, 0.0), scale: 1.3),
    "chocolate_bar": (offset: (0.12, 0.0, -0.04), scale: 1.3),
}
